      "side": 1,
      "message": "Gemini feedback:\n\n-----\n\nHere is a complete inventory of every place in the patch where `.value()` is used to unwrap `std::expected` (and `std::optional`, which shares the exact same pointer-like idiom).\n\nBy replacing `.value()` with `*` (dereference) or `-\u003e` (member access), the code becomes significantly cleaner and visually separates *error checking* from *value extraction*.\n\n### 1. The \"Inline Conditional\" Upgrades\n\nWhen you call a function that returns `std::expected` and only need the value if it succeeds, you can declare, check, and unwrap it all in one clean `if` statement using `-\u003e`.\n\n**`et171_flash.cc`**\n\n* *Current:*\n```cpp\nif (auto info_res \u003d brom.GetBootromInfo(); info_res) {\n  auto \u0026info \u003d info_res.value();\n  std::println(\"Bootrom Version: 0x{:x}\", info.version);\n\n```\n\n\n\n```\n    *Idiomatic:*\n    ```cpp\n    if (auto info \u003d brom.GetBootromInfo()) {\n      std::println(\"Bootrom Version: 0x{:x}\", info-\u003eversion);\n\n```\n\n* *Current:*\n```cpp\nif (auto flash_res \u003d brom.GetFlashInfo(); flash_res) {\n  auto \u0026flash \u003d flash_res.value();\n  std::println(\"  Product Name: {}\", MakeStringView(flash.prod_name));\n\n```\n\n\n\n```\n    *Idiomatic:*\n    ```cpp\n    if (auto flash \u003d brom.GetFlashInfo()) {\n      std::println(\"  Product Name: {}\", MakeStringView(flash-\u003eprod_name));\n\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Standard Pointer-Like Unwrapping\n\nIn these locations, the `expected` or `optional` has already been checked for errors. You can replace `.value()` directly with `*`.\n\n**`bootrom.cc`**\n\n* *Current:* `if (!read_res || read_res.value() \u003c\u003d 0)`\n*Idiomatic:* `if (!read_res || *read_res \u003c\u003d 0)`\n* *Current:* `ret.resize(read_res.value());`\n*Idiomatic:* `ret.resize(*read_res);`\n* *Current:* `if (status.value() !\u003d 0)`\n*Idiomatic:* `if (*status !\u003d 0)`\n* *Current:* `auto \u0026ret \u003d ret_res.value();` *(Used in `SendBootromCommandRaw` and `SendBootromCommandSha`)*\n*Idiomatic:* `auto \u0026ret \u003d *ret_res;`\n* *Current:* `secure_data \u003d extracted.value();`\n*Idiomatic:* `secure_data \u003d *extracted;`\n* *Current:* `if ((sr1.value() \u0026 EgisBootrom::kFlashSr1Wip) \u003d\u003d 0)`\n*Idiomatic:* `if ((*sr1 \u0026 EgisBootrom::kFlashSr1Wip) \u003d\u003d 0)`\n* *Current:* `return FromLittleEndian(value_out.value());`\n*Idiomatic:* `return FromLittleEndian(*value_out);`\n* *Current:* `return static_cast\u003cuint8_t\u003e(res.value() \u0026 0xFF);`\n*Idiomatic:* `return static_cast\u003cuint8_t\u003e(*res \u0026 0xFF);`\n* *Current:* `std::println(\"Old SR1: 0x{:02x}\", sr1_old_res.value());` (and `sr1_new_res`)\n*Idiomatic:* `std::println(\"Old SR1: 0x{:02x}\", *sr1_old_res);`\n* *Current:* `EgisBootrom::BootromInfoResponse info \u003d info_res.value();`\n*Idiomatic:* `auto info \u003d *info_res;`\n* *Current:* `EgisBootrom::FlashInfoResponse info \u003d info_res.value();`\n*Idiomatic:* `auto info \u003d *info_res;`\n\n**`ec_comm.cc` \u0026 `ec_comm.h**`\n\n* *Current:* `size_t rx_size \u003d actual_res.value();`\n*Idiomatic:* `size_t rx_size \u003d *actual_res;`\n* *Current:* `auto resp_hdr \u003d ReadStruct\u003c...\u003e(resp_buf).value();`\n*Idiomatic:* `auto resp_hdr \u003d *ReadStruct\u003c...\u003e(resp_buf);`\n* *Current:* `return parsed.value();`\n*Idiomatic:* `return *parsed;`\n\n**`file_util.cc`**\n\n* *Current:* `auto \u0026key_opt \u003d key_res.value();`\n*Idiomatic:* `auto \u0026key_opt \u003d *key_res;`\n\n**`flasher_logic.cc`**\n\n* *Current:* `if (!packet_size_res || packet_size_res.value() \u003e firmware.size())`\n*Idiomatic:* `if (!packet_size_res || *packet_size_res \u003e firmware.size())`\n* *Current:* `size_t take \u003d packet_size_res.value();`\n*Idiomatic:* `size_t take \u003d *packet_size_res;`\n* *Current:* `if (!read_res || read_res.value() \u003c\u003d 0)`\n*Idiomatic:* `if (!read_res || *read_res \u003c\u003d 0)`\n* *Current:* `if (read_res.value() \u003e\u003d BootromComm::kStatusHeaderSize)`\n*Idiomatic:* `if (*read_res \u003e\u003d BootromComm::kStatusHeaderSize)`\n* *Current:* `if (status \u0026\u0026 status.value() !\u003d 0)`\n*Idiomatic:* `if (status \u0026\u0026 *status !\u003d 0)`\n\n**`et171_flash.cc` (Including `std::optional` instances)**\n\n* *Current:* `GetVersionResponse response \u003d resp.value();`\n*Idiomatic:* `auto response \u003d *resp;`\n* *Current:* `const egis::AppConfig \u0026config \u003d config_opt.value();`\n*Idiomatic:* `const auto \u0026config \u003d *config_opt;`\n* *Current:* `app_profile.id.pid \u003d config.pid.value();`\n*Idiomatic:* `app_profile.id.pid \u003d *config.pid;`\n\n**`usb_comm.cc`**\n\n* *Current:* `if (!res || res.value() !\u003d static_cast\u003cint\u003e(data.size()))`\n*Idiomatic:* `if (!res || *res !\u003d static_cast\u003cint\u003e(data.size()))`\n\n**`cli_options.cc` (`std::optional`)**\n\n* *Current:* `if (opt \u003d\u003d \u0027o\u0027) config.flash_offset \u003d parsed_val.value();`\n*Idiomatic:* `if (opt \u003d\u003d \u0027o\u0027) config.flash_offset \u003d *parsed_val;`\n* *Current:* `if (opt \u003d\u003d \u0027s\u0027) config.fw_size_override \u003d parsed_val.value();`\n*Idiomatic:* `if (opt \u003d\u003d \u0027s\u0027) config.fw_size_override \u003d *parsed_val;`\n* *Current:* `config.pid \u003d parsed_val.value();`\n*Idiomatic:* `config.pid \u003d *parsed_val;`\n\n---\n\n### 3. Cleaning Up the Tests\n\nTest files are fantastic places to use pointer semantics because it makes the assertions read much more naturally.\n\n**`bootrom_test.cc` \u0026 `ec_comm_test.cc` \u0026 `cli_options_test.cc**`\n\n* *Current:* `EXPECT_TRUE(std::ranges::equal(kTestPlaintext, res.value()));`\n*Idiomatic:* `EXPECT_TRUE(std::ranges::equal(kTestPlaintext, *res));`\n* *Current:* `EXPECT_EQ(res.value().size(), total_size);`\n*Idiomatic:* `EXPECT_EQ(res-\u003esize(), total_size);`\n* *Current:* `EXPECT_EQ(res.value()[0], 0xAA);`\n*Idiomatic:* `EXPECT_EQ((*res)[0], 0xAA);`\n* *Current:* `EXPECT_EQ(config-\u003edump_cmd_path.value(), \"cmd.bin\");`\n*Idiomatic:* `EXPECT_EQ(*config-\u003edump_cmd_path, \"cmd.bin\");`\n* *Current:* `EXPECT_EQ(config-\u003epid.value(), 0x1234);`\n*Idiomatic:* `EXPECT_EQ(*config-\u003epid, 0x1234);`",
