      "side": 1,
      "message": "Gemini feedback:\n\n----\n\nIn `bootrom.cc` (`WaitForFlashReady`) and `et171_flash.cc` (`ConnectToBootloader`), you are calculating timeouts by doing repeated time arithmetic on every iteration of a `while` loop:\n\n```c\nauto start_time \u003d std::chrono::steady_clock::now();\nwhile (std::chrono::steady_clock::now() - start_time \u003c timeout) {\n    // ...\n\n```\n\nWhile this works, it requires the CPU to do a subtraction and a comparison on every tick. The idiomatic C++ `std::chrono` approach is to calculate an **absolute deadline** once before the loop begins.\n\n**The Fix:**\n\n```c\nauto deadline \u003d std::chrono::steady_clock::now() + timeout;\nwhile (std::chrono::steady_clock::now() \u003c deadline) {\n    // ...\n\n```\n\nThis is computationally cheaper, impossible to get the subtraction order wrong, and clearly reads as \"while now is before the deadline.\"",
