      "message": "Gemini feedback:\n\n-----\n\nIn `bootrom_protocol.h`, you very cleanly define default values for your hardware structs. For example:\n\n```c\nstruct MemReadCommand {\n  CommandId command_id \u003d CommandId::kMemRead;\n  uint32_t address;\n  AccessSize access_size;\n  uint32_t count;\n} __attribute__((packed));\n\n```\n\nHowever, in `bootrom.cc`, you are manually redefining the `.command_id` (and sometimes `.access_size`) every time you instantiate the structs:\n\n```c\n  EgisBootrom::MemReadCommand req{\n      .command_id \u003d EgisBootrom::CommandId::kMemRead, // \u003c-- Redundant\n      .address \u003d ToLittleEndian(flash_addr),\n      .access_size \u003d EgisBootrom::AccessSize::kUint8,\n      .count \u003d ToLittleEndian(take)};\n\n```\n\nC++20 designated initializers automatically fall back to the default member initializers defined in the struct. You can delete the redundant `.command_id` lines across the entire codebase to make the payloads much cleaner to read:\n\n```c\n  EgisBootrom::MemReadCommand req{\n      .address \u003d ToLittleEndian(flash_addr),\n      .access_size \u003d EgisBootrom::AccessSize::kUint8,\n      .count \u003d ToLittleEndian(take)};\n\n```",
