      "message": "Gemini feedback:\n\n----\n\nIn `bootrom.cc` (`BackupFlash`) and `flasher_logic.cc` (`ProgramFlashPayload` and `ProgramRawCommandPayload`), you repeat the exact same progress bar calculation, formatting, and flush logic three times:\n\n```c\n  size_t done \u003d total_size - payload.size();\n  std::print(\"\\rWriting Progress: {} / {} ({:.1f}%)\", done, total_size,\n             (static_cast\u003cfloat\u003e(done) / total_size * 100.0f));\n  std::fflush(stdout);\n\n```\n\n**The Fix:** Centralize this into `egis_util.h` (or a dedicated `ui_util.h`). If you ever want to change how progress looks (e.g., adding a visual bar `[\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003e   ]`), you only have to update it in one place.\n\n**In `egis_util.h`:**\n\n```c\ninline void PrintProgress(std::string_view prefix, size_t done, size_t total) {\n  if (total \u003d\u003d 0) return;\n  std::print(\"\\r{}: {} / {} ({:.1f}%)\", prefix, done, total,\n             (static_cast\u003cfloat\u003e(done) / total * 100.0f));\n  std::fflush(stdout);\n}\n\n```\n\nNow, your flasher loops become perfectly clean one-liners:\n\n```c\n  PrintProgress(\"Flashing Progress\", total_size - firmware.size(), total_size);\n\n```",
