      "side": 1,
      "message": "Gemini feedback:\n\n----\n\nAcross `bootrom.h`, `ec_comm.h`, `usb_interface.h`, and `crypto_util.h`, you implement `ToString(ErrorEnum)` functions using `switch` statements with a `default:` case:\n\n```c\nconstexpr std::string_view ToString(BootromError err) {\n  switch (err) {\n    case BootromError::kUsbWriteFailed: return \"USB write failed\";\n    // ...\n    default: return \"An unknown error occurred\";\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n**The Issue:** By including a `default:` case, you suppress the compiler\u0027s `-Wswitch` warning. If a future maintainer adds a new enum value (e.g., `BootromError::kVerificationFailed`), the compiler *will not warn them* that they forgot to update the stringifier, leading to blind spots in your logs.\n\n**The Fix:** Remove the `default:` label and put the fallback return *outside* the `switch` block. This forces the compiler to statically verify that every single enum value is explicitly handled in the `switch`.\n\n```c\nconstexpr std::string_view ToString(BootromError err) {\n  switch (err) {\n    case BootromError::kUsbWriteFailed: return \"USB write failed\";\n    // ... all explicitly defined cases ...\n  }\n  // The compiler will warn if a new enum is added but missed above!\n  return \"An unknown error occurred\"; \n}\n\n```",
