      "message": "In `bootrom_protocol.h`, you enclose the hardware definitions in a capitalized namespace:\n\n```c\nnamespace egis::EgisBootrom {\n\n```\n\n**The Issue:** The Google C++ Style Guide explicitly states: *\"Namespace names are all lower-case, with words separated by underscores.\"* (e.g., `mac_address_table`). Capitalized names are strictly reserved for Types and Classes.\n\n**The Fix:** Rename the inner namespace to snake\\_case.\n\n```c\nnamespace egis::bootrom_protocol {\n\n```\n\n*(You will then update usages like `EgisBootrom::CommandId` to `bootrom_protocol::CommandId` across the codebase).*",
