      "message": "Gemini feedback:\n\n----\n\nIn `bootrom_protocol.h`, `SecureCommandBaseHeader` stores the cryptographic algorithm as a raw `uint8_t`:\n\n```c\nstruct SecureCommandBaseHeader {\n  CommandId command_id \u003d CommandId::kSecureWrapped;\n  uint8_t algo; // \u003c--- Raw integer\n  uint32_t payload_len;\n} __attribute__((packed));\n\n```\n\nThis forces you to use `std::to_underlying` or `static_cast\u003cuint8_t\u003e` every time you build the header in `bootrom.cc`.\n\nBecause you explicitly defined the underlying type of `EgisCryptoType` as `uint8_t` (`enum class EgisCryptoType : uint8_t`), C++ allows you to use the enum directly inside packed structs. It will still compile down to exactly 1 byte on the wire.\n\n**The Fix:**\n\n```c\nstruct SecureCommandBaseHeader {\n  CommandId command_id \u003d CommandId::kSecureWrapped;\n  EgisCryptoType algo; // \u003c--- Strongly typed\n  uint32_t payload_len;\n} __attribute__((packed));\n\n```\n\nNow, in `bootrom.cc`, you can assign it natively: `req_hdr.algo \u003d wrapped_algo_;`",
