      "message": "Gemini feedback:\n\n----\n\nI mentioned this previously for `PackMessage`, but it applies across several other files (like `bootrom.cc` and `bootrom_test.cc`). You are using the legacy `\u003cvector\u003e` idiom of calling `.insert()` with `.begin()` and `.end()` iterators:\n\n```c\nbuffer.insert(buffer.end(), resp-\u003ebegin(), resp-\u003eend());\n\n// In bootrom_test.cc:\nresp_packet.insert(resp_packet.end(), tag.begin(), tag.end());\nresp_packet.insert(resp_packet.end(), ciphertext.begin(), ciphertext.end());\n\n```\n\n**The Fix:** C++23 introduced `std::vector::append_range`, which accepts any range (like `std::vector`, `std::array`, or `std::span`) directly. This is safer, more performant, and drastically more readable:\n\n```c\nbuffer.append_range(*resp);\n\n// In bootrom_test.cc:\nresp_packet.append_range(tag);\nresp_packet.append_range(ciphertext);\n\n```",
