      "message": "Gemini feedback:\n\n----\n\nIn your tests (`bootrom_test.cc`, `ec_comm_test.cc`), you verify payload equivalence using standard ranges:\n\n```c\nEXPECT_TRUE(std::ranges::equal(kTestPlaintext, *res));\n\n```\n\n**The Issue:** If this test fails on a CI server, GoogleTest will output: `Expected: true` `Actual: false` You will have absolutely no idea *which* bytes mismatched, forcing you to run the test locally with a debugger.\n\n**The Fix:** Include `\u003cgmock/gmock.h\u003e` and leverage GoogleTest\u0027s native container matchers. It natively understands `std::vector`, `std::array`, and `std::span`.\n\n```c\n#include \u003cgmock/gmock.h\u003e\n\n// Inside the test:\nEXPECT_THAT(*res, ::testing::ElementsAreArray(kTestPlaintext));\n\n```\n\nIf this fails, GoogleTest will now print a beautiful diff showing the exact index and hex values where the arrays diverged, saving hours of debugging time.",
