      "side": 1,
      "message": "Gemini feedback:\n\n-----\n\nIn `ec_comm.cc`, you define a full class (`EcCommand`) with private members and an accessor, solely to pack a struct and vector together exactly once. This is a classic C++ anti-pattern where a simple sequence of statements is wrapped in unnecessary Object-Oriented boilerplate.\n\nYou can delete the entire `EcCommand` class definition and inline the logic directly into `SendCommand`, saving \\~15 lines and making the function flow linearly.\n\n**In `ec_comm.cc`:**\n\n```c\n// 1. Delete the entire class EcCommand { ... }; block.\n\n// 2. Rewrite SendCommand:\nstd::expected\u003cstd::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e, EcError\u003e EcComm::SendCommand(\n    uint16_t cmd_id, uint8_t cmd_ver, std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e payload) {\n  \n  if (payload.size() \u003e std::numeric_limits\u003cuint16_t\u003e::max()) {\n    std::println(stderr, \"[FATAL] EC command payload exceeds limit.\");\n    std::abort();\n  }\n\n  EcHostCommandRequest hdr \u003d {\n      .command_id \u003d ToLittleEndian(cmd_id),\n      .command_version \u003d cmd_ver,\n      .data_length \u003d ToLittleEndian(static_cast\u003cuint16_t\u003e(payload.size()))};\n\n  auto tx_bytes \u003d PackMessage(hdr, payload);\n  ApplyEcChecksum(tx_bytes);\n\n  if (auto res \u003d usb_.Send(tx_bytes); !res) {\n    std::println(stderr, \"[ERROR] Failed to send EC command: {}\", ToString(res.error()));\n    return std::unexpected(EcError::kUsbSendFailed);\n  }\n  \n  // ... rest of the receive logic remains unchanged\n}\n\n```",
