      "message": "Gemini feedback:\n\n-----\n\nIn `flasher_logic.cc` (`ProgramRawCommandPayload`), you are manually making `boot_comm.Send()` and `boot_comm.Receive()` calls, and then manually unpacking and verifying the 2-byte little-endian status header.\n\nThis breaks encapsulation: **`BootromComm::DoUsbTransfer` already does exactly this.**\n\nInstead of rewriting the USB response validation logic in the flasher, you should promote `DoUsbTransfer` to a public method on `BootromComm` (perhaps renamed to `SendPrewrappedPacket`) and inject `BootromComm` into `RunFlashCmd` instead of raw `UsbInterface`.\n\n**In `bootrom.h` (move from private to public and rename):**\n\n```cpp\n  std::expected\u003cstd::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e, BootromError\u003e SendPrewrappedPacket(\n      std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e tx_cmd, size_t min_expected_rx_size \u003d 0,\n      std::chrono::milliseconds timeout \u003d kDefaultCommandTimeout);\n\n```\n\n**Now `ProgramRawCommandPayload` (in `flasher_logic.cc`) becomes drastically simpler:**\n\n```cpp\nstd::expected\u003cvoid, AppError\u003e ProgramRawCommandPayload(\n    BootromComm \u0026brom, std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e firmware) {  // \u003c-- Takes BootromComm now\n  std::println(\"--- Flash RAW CMD Binary Flashing ---\");\n  const size_t total_size \u003d firmware.size();\n\n  while (!firmware.empty()) {\n    auto packet_size_res \u003d GetNextPacketSize(firmware);\n    size_t offset \u003d total_size - firmware.size();\n\n    if (!packet_size_res || packet_size_res.value() \u003e firmware.size()) {\n      std::println(stderr, \"\\n[ERROR] Parse failed/truncated at offset 0x{:X}\", offset);\n      return std::unexpected(AppError::kParseError);\n    }\n\n    size_t take \u003d packet_size_res.value();\n    std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e packet \u003d firmware.first(take);\n    firmware \u003d firmware.subspan(take);\n\n    // If it\u0027s a reset, just send it raw\n    if (packet[0] \u003d\u003d std::to_underlying(EgisBootrom::CommandId::kSystemReset)) {\n       brom.SystemReset(); // \u003c-- Reusing existing BootromComm logic\n       continue;\n    }\n\n    // Send it through BootromComm, which handles the USB receive and Status Header validation automatically!\n    if (auto res \u003d brom.SendPrewrappedPacket(packet); !res) {\n      std::println(stderr, \"\\n[ERROR] Device error at 0x{:X}: {}\", offset, ToString(res.error()));\n      return std::unexpected(AppError::kBootromError);\n    }\n\n    size_t done \u003d total_size - firmware.size();\n    std::print(\"\\rFlashing Progress: {} / {} ({:.1f}%)\", done, total_size,\n               (static_cast\u003cfloat\u003e(done) / total_size * 100.0f));\n    std::fflush(stdout);\n  }\n\n  std::println(\"\\n[OK] RAW CMD Flashing Finished\");\n  return {};\n}\n\n```\n\n*Don\u0027t forget to update the signature of `RunFlashCmd` in `flasher_logic.h`/`.cc` and `et171_flash.cc` to pass `brom` instead of `boot_comm`.*",
